 "files": [
  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Squeeze In\n\nCharacters are uncovered one by one by a clean wipe, then the whole word squeezes tighter as the last one lands.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A wordmark or short title should be uncovered by a clean wipe, as if a cover slid off it.\n- The arrival of the last character should compress every letter gap, so the word settles tighter.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The word should collapse from a wide tracked-out state with blur: use tracking-in.\n- Characters should rise or drop into place: use per-character-rise or top-down-letters.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Studio\"\n- stagger (number, 1-8): Stagger, default 3\n- squeeze (number, 0-0.2): Squeeze, default 0.03\n- font_size (number, 12-160): Font size, default 72\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"400\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Squeeze In\n\n  Characters are uncovered one by one by a clean wipe, then the whole word squeezes tighter as the last one lands.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/squeeze-in/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"squeeze-in\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Word or short title.\", \"default\": \"Studio\" },\n    { \"id\": \"stagger\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Stagger\", \"description\": \"Frames per character while the wipe uncovers it (30 fps).\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 8, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"squeeze\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Squeeze\", \"description\": \"How wide the letter gaps start, as a fraction of the font size. They close to zero.\", \"default\": 0.03, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 0.2, \"step\": 0.005 },\n    { \"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 72, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 160, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"400\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}] }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Squeeze In</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          color: var(--color, #171717);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .sqz-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          display: flex;\n          align-items: center;\n          justify-content: center;\n        }\n        .sqz-line { display: inline-block; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.1; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .sqz-char { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"squeeze-in\" data-duration=\"2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"sqz-clip\" class=\"sqz-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"sqz-line\" class=\"sqz-line\" role=\"img\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function bz(id, a, b, c, d) {\n              return CustomEase.create(\"sqz-\" + id, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            // interpolate(frame, [a, b], [from, to], { easing }) as a tween (frames at 30 fps).\n            function tw(tl, el, from, to, a, b, ease, keep) {\n              var t = Object.assign({}, to, { duration: (b - a) / 30, ease: ease || \"none\", immediateRender: !keep });\n              tl.fromTo(el, from, t, a / 30);\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font size so it fits a fraction of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, frac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\n            function finish(tl) {\n              if (tl.duration() < TOTAL) tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"squeeze-in\"] = tl;\n            }\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Studio\");\n            var weight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"400\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            // interpolate() with clamping, easing given as a function of progress.\n            function ip(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n\n            var stagger = num(vars.stagger, 3, 1, 8);\n            var squeeze = num(vars.squeeze, 0.03, 0, 0.2);\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"sqz-line\");\n            line.style.fontWeight = weight;\n            line.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            var chars = Array.from(text).map(function (ch, i) {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.id = \"sqz-char-\" + i;\n              s.className = \"sqz-char\";\n              s.textContent = ch;\n              line.appendChild(s);\n              return s;\n            });\n            var size = fit(line, num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 160), 0.9);\n\n            var out = bz(\"out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var lastReveal = chars.length * stagger;\n            var P = { f: 0 };\n            function apply() {\n              var f = P.f;\n              var prog = ip(f, lastReveal, lastReveal + 16, 0, 1, out);\n              var wipe = ip(f, 0, lastReveal, 100, 0);\n              var gap = squeeze * size * (1 - prog);\n              chars.forEach(function (c, j) {\n                c.style.marginRight = j < chars.length - 1 ? gap + \"px\" : \"0px\";\n              });\n              line.style.transform = \"translate(\" + (-squeeze * size * prog * (chars.length - 1)) / 2 + \"px, 0)\";\n              line.style.clipPath = \"inset(-0.2em \" + wipe + \"% -0.25em -0.1em)\";\n            }\n            apply();\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(P, { f: lastReveal + 16, duration: (lastReveal + 16) / 30, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: apply }, 0);\n            finish(tl);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
